From a82ee9fefb178e4f5331f2db7ac590b5c4e4b92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sang Woo Kim <physwkim@postech.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 10:10:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] probe(pvalink-stage5): the on-target two-IOC measurement
 image
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measurement scaffolding for doc/pvalink-rtems-design.md §5 stage 5,
topology A. NOT for merge — the same arrangement as
doc/rtems-priority-probe.patch and the slirp probe: the probe lives in
its own commit on the branch that produced the measurement document.

Three parts, each forced by something the target does not have:

* `EPICS_PVA_NAME_SERVERS` is compiled in. `rtems_init.c:195` hands
  `main` a fixed one-element argv and POSIX_Init calls `setenv` zero
  times, so there is no environment and no command line to configure the
  guest with. Set before `install_pvalink_resolver` builds the ONE
  client, whose builder reads the variable once at construction.
* The two link-bearing records live in DEMO_DB. A `-kernel` boot has no
  filesystem, so there is no path a `.db` argument could name.
* A console reporter thread, because criterion 6 asks for `rt top` /
  `rt stackuse` on an image that configures the shell's commands but
  starts no shell. The C side calls the same
  `rtems_stack_checker_report_usage` the shell's `stackuse` calls, and
  reuses the task census from doc/rtems-priority-probe.patch verbatim.

`PvaLinkResolver::client_report` / `PvaLinkRegistry::client` are the
guest-side view of "one upstream connection regardless of link count".
---
